WEBVTT

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:23.670
I want to...

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.340
...revitalize our village.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.300
Revitalizing the village...

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.470
That sounds great!

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:38.140
Anyone have any ideas?

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.720
Revitalizing the village...

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.770
Let's see...

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.230
Ah! I gotta go!

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:12.170
Oh, that was in the design competition!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.420
It was number one!

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.260
You look great, Machi!

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.720
The mountain gods probably love it too.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:20.310
What? How do you know about that?

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.060
Well, you see...

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.190
Now she's tried them all.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.690
Which was best, judges?

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.150
I like number two.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.440
Huh?

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.570
I can't say I agree.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.070
I do appreciate the ears and tail,

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.450
but it's not that good, really.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.410
Don't push.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.700
I can't see.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.330
I'm all for number three.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.330
You're heavy!

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.040
Uh, you know...

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.330
Yoshio showed us some pictures.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:47.960
Right?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:48.830
Yeah.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:51.090
I liked number four.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:52.710
Number four was awesome.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:01:59.970
Yeah, I liked that one.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.350
Me, too.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.930
Hey, what about number three?

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.350
Number three?

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.230
Number three sucked.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.620
Yoshio, is Natsu upset because we were chit-chatting?

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.750
Please forgive us. Please forgive us. Please forgive us.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.680
Number two was good, too.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.720
It was kind of fancy.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.060
Yeah.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.140
Seeing them in person, number one's sheer sleeves work really well.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.440
I hear it's called "thoo-serou."

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.730
No, it's "see-through."

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.780
Oh, that's right. See-through. See-through.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.650
Dummies.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.910
It's raining!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.410
Let's finish this quick and go home!

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.790
This is a blessing from the mountain gods!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.010
So, though it is a bit later than usual,

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:56.440
we've finished planting the rice and
performed a prayer for a bountiful harvest.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.610
Let's toast to a good crop! Cheers!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.900
Cheers!

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.170
Hm? You're wearing that outfit?

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.800
I'd wear my usual one,
but I took it to get cleaned today

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.170
since I planned on wearing the other one all day.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.380
Oh. I see.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:28.680
Number four's all right, too.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.930
Hey! Good work out there!

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.100
You too, Yoshio.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.770
The old guys gave us this for lunch.

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.400
It's your favorite, Natsu. Sushi!

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.190
Whoa!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:45.360
Boy, I'm starving! I'm gonna dig in!

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:47.320
No! I call the salmon!

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:55.200
Natsu, you'd better start eating or Machi will eat all your favorites.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.210
Know what?

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.590
I think it's a waste that we have this lovely girl,

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:07.510
dancing and doing exorcisms,
but it's not open to the public.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.130
"Lovely"...

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.090
I agree.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:13.010
We can't show Natsu to the public, can we?

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.640
He even performs kagura with me.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.600
I don't have to appear in public.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:22.690
We could have a villager disguised as a bear instead.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.480
Oh, that's a good idea!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.150
What?! I'm not doing anything without Natsu.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:31.910
It's not fair if I have to work and he doesn't!

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.160
Ah. That takes me back...

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.500
There!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.460
So that's how it is?

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.670
Then take this!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:48.300
If you only play with me, you won't be able to make human friends.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.430
That's okay.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.890
Only you is fine!

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.060
What are you doing, Natsu? That's creepy.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.070
Machi, can you survive without Natsu?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:04.900
What?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:09.320
<i>I don't know why, but that's a very annoying question.</i>

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:14.080
How rude! Natsu is the one who can't do anything without me!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.700
See? He's got rice on his cheek.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.580
Well, as long as you're okay, but can you please consider public performances?

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.880
Just for events like the performing arts festival,

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.960
or the fall festival at Yamaoku Park...

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.840
I won't. It's embarrassing and too much work.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.810
It'll be fine. Give it a shot, Machi.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.520
No. You're not doing it, so I won't, either.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.930
What?

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.280
Well then, I'm going back to
cleaning up the community center.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.490
Hold on. Yoshio, do you understand me?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.950
What're you talking about? Of course I do.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.830
Wait, Yoshio!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.120
Yoshio!

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.790
Oh, shoot! They're waiting on me.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.540
What're you doing?!

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:05.540
Hey!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.500
See you! Finish up the sushi, okay?

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.300
Yoshio!

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.680
Do you think he really understood?

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.180
<i>He's up to something silly.</i>

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.940
Now that lunch is done,

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.440
I'm gonna go finish cleaning.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.520
I'll start with the shed.

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:38.740
<i>Still...</i>

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:43.120
<i>Something's bothering me.</i>

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.210
Machi, can you survive without Natsu?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.220
<i>I can't survive without Natsu?!</i>

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.310
<i>That's not true.</i>

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:11.440
Today's superb gourmet food is full of seasonal fruits.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:11.440
<i>I can use the TV by myself.</i>

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.950
Channel 2

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.950
<i>I even know how to change inputs.</i>

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.830
<i>I can venture out of the town</i>

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:27.630
<i>and explore caves, too.</i>

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:32.020
Ahh!

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.310
<i>That's enough adventure for today.</i>

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.860
<i>What about Natsu?</i>

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.940
<i>Doesn't he depend on me to survive?</i>

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:02.950
<i>Aw, see? The ladder isn't steady.</i>

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.700
<i>He'll fall. Someday, he'll fall.</i>

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:13.090
<i>Natsu can't lock the door.</i>

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.590
<i>But he still tries, since he hates to admit he can't.</i>

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.760
<i>But he always ends up asking me to—</i>

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.230
<i>What did he just do?</i>

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.990
<i>It's locked!</i>

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:43.990
<i>Natsu...</i>

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.620
<i>With his bear hands...</i>

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.540
<i>He must have worked so hard.</i>

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.210
<i>I thought you'd always have a bear's paws,</i>

00:10:54.210 --> 00:10:56.260
<i>but you've evolved, haven't you?</i>

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.890
<i>It stings a bit, but I should congratulate him.</i>

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:06.520
Natsu...

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:07.430
Hm?

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.270
Natsu, the lock on the shed...

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:16.530
Oh, that. It's amazing, isn't it? Yoshio set things up.

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.530
It became a keyless entry!

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.110
What? Oh... yeah...

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.240
So you became a keyless entry, huh?! You're amazing, Natsu!

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.240
Became?

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.520
Hey, Yoshio's cousin.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.780
Do you still spend all your time with that bear?

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:09.450
Hey!

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.630
You asleep or something?

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.340
Did you not hear my question?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:21.550
Machi! Machi! Get a hold of yourself, Machi!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.970
It's an everyday thing to be
harassed by punks in rural areas.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.180
There's no point in trying to reason with them.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:31.480
I have to find a way out of this absurd situation.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.480
Boys picked on me all the time when I was young.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.360
This isn't enough to break me!

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.230
I'll survive, no matter what! I'll survive!

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:41.690
Hm?

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.280
Hey! You gonna sit there forever?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.660
Wai— Hey!

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>Did I kick her that hard?</i>

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.170
Ah! Don't run from me! Hey!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.680
Ow!

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.430
There's no reason to run away, <i>okay</i>?

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:15.940
Why don't you get along with your Big sis...

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.860
and talk with her

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.900
a little bit?

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.360
What?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:28.910
Wa—

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:29.740
"Wa"?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.620
Wahhh!

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.580
Natsu! Natsu! Natsu! Natsu!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:35.120
Hey!

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.960
Natsu! Natsu! Natsu!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.330
Natsuu!

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.250
Naatsuuu!

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.250
What's wrong?

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.510
Natsu! Natsu! Natsu! Natsu!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.510
Amazing! There's still reception out here.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:48.220
Natsu! Natsu! Natsu!

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.640
Ah! Hibiki's bullying Machi!

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:51.640
Natsu!

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:56.640
Poor thing. She's scared senseless.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.060
What'd you do to her, Hibiki?!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.730
Ah! She's covered in dirt.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.570
Were you beating her or what?!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:06.400
She started rolling around on her own!

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.160
Now see here, I don't know what your intent was,

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.280
but I can't ignore you hurting Machi, Hibiki!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.790
I wasn't intending anything.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.790
I just want to talk to her!

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:21.590
Oh, really? You're easily misunderstood, aren't you?

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.750
Can it!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.710
Don't worry, Machi.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:28.050
Hibiki just uses rough body language, that's all.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.050
She's used to getting physical.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.310
If you brace yourself, it won't hurt much.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:37.810
We already know each other! Why is she acting like that?

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.810
For a delicate girl getting harassed by a thug,

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.820
it doesn't matter if she knows you or not.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.150
It's been so long since you last came,

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.200
but you still haven't broken that bad habit of yours.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:52.570
You think I'm going to listen to a bear?

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:56.410
Don't get ahead of yourself! What's up with these glasses?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.460
So what do you want with Machi?

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.830
Oh, right.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.380
The two of us became close friends earlier.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.710
So we're gonna go out shopping together.

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:07.710
Huh?

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:09.800
We are going window shopping.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.220
What? Really?!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.680
That sounds great!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.720
Right?

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.810
She said she doesn't have many clothes.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.730
You can't take her, right?

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.440
N-No thank y—

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.520
Huh?!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.480
Thank you for taking me.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.360
Wow.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.950
You're really going shopping together.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.830
That's so girly!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.580
See you later.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:42.710
Have fun!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.710
Why?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.710
Why?!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:15.660
Hibiki...

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.660
Yeah?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:18.660
Is this where we're shopping?

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:20.410
That it is.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.120
Welcome!

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.880
<i>The store is spacious and bright.</i>

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:32.590
<i>Uniformed store employees...</i>

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.340
Maintaining an appropriate distance...

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:36.550
<i>And granite flooring!</i>

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:40.810
<i>Ah... This place makes me feel comfortable.</i>

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.520
I see!

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:47.020
Hibiki buys her clothes at Shimomura, too.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.860
Everyone shops at Shimomura, after all.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.410
Wh-Why?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:00.370
Something about your smile pissed me off.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.370
Go on! Hurry up and pick something!

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:06.830
Just put everything you like in the basket.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.880
I'll pick out what's the best.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.210
Stuff here's cheap, so don't worry about picking wrong!

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.670
The budget is 20,000 yen! My treat.

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:15.010
What?!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.050
I came across a good chunk of money recently.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:20.100
<i>That's suspicious!</i>

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:24.230
That's not right. I can't have you pay for me.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:25.890
I don't even know why we're he—

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:32.480
Just shut up and be my dress-up doll, okay?!

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:32.480
Yes ma'am.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:35.360
<i>I'm going to be a doll for the rest of my life.</i>

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:43.160
<i>Now that I think about it, I haven't been to this Shimomura in a while.</i>

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:46.790
<i>It looks kinda different now.</i>

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.920
<i>When I was a kid, only moms shopped here.</i>

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:53.800
Shimomura never seems to stop growing, does it?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:54.970
Hm?

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:56.680
There are 1,500 stores.

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:59.340
It's expanded to markets beyond Japan.

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:02.470
Shimomura is a Japanese icon in the fast fashion industry,

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.020
and its sales make it a market leader.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.730
Their management style is so good,

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:12.320
they can spend 100 million yen on a 10,000 square foot space

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.990
and break even within three years.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:20.820
Isn't it awe-inspiring to realize they
invested that much out here in the boonies?

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.700
<i>What's her deal?</i>

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.000
<i>Secret agent for Shimomura?</i>

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.040
Oh, is that so?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:30.420
I thought it was just a cheap clothing store,

00:18:30.420 --> 00:18:31.880
but it's way bigger than that, huh?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.460
Hibiki, do you know...

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:37.090
...how their clothes are so cheap?

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:42.220
It's not because the clothes are made cheaply, or they found a cheap supplier.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:46.310
It's due to their cost-cutting strategy, cultivated over many years

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.850
and still improving even now.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:52.610
Their affordable prices are made possible

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:56.030
because their employees are highly efficient.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.650
<i>What is this? Who is she?</i>

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:08.370
So I have to question people when they simply lump Shimomura into "fast fashion."

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.500
<i>The look in her eyes has changed.</i>

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:14.130
<i>Come to think of it, she's a miko, right?</i>

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:17.010
<i>Has something descended into her?</i>

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.970
<i>The god of apparel?!</i>

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.350
W-Well, whatever.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.890
It's no fun standing around.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.600
Maybe I'll find something for myself, too.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:34.650
Yes. Every store stocks more than 50,000 items.

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:37.530
I'm sure you'll find something that's perfect for you.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:40.900
<i>Why does she know these minor details about everything?</i>

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.280
<i>Oh? These are nice.</i>

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.660
<i>And they're only 1500 yen?</i>

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.000
<i>Feels like treasure hunting.</i>

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.250
Hibiki.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.840
Have you noticed that everything in your basket

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:59.170
has the same brand?

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.680
They do! YH...

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:06.180
Shimomura has exclusive
distribution rights for that brand.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:07.680
YH is...

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:13.560
<i>Yamano Hiroko?!</i>

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:19.280
<i>My impression of Shimomura has totally changed.</i>

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.740
<i>Even though the logo hasn't.</i>

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:27.910
Ugh! They've only got large for this, but I'm medium!

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:33.500
Each store only gets a few of each size of an item, so when they sell out, that's it.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.670
In return, they get new items every day.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:41.260
Really... Then I guess I won't get this.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:44.680
Hibiki, it's too soon to give up.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.350
Shimomura...

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:51.180
...has another store in the neighboring town.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:56.020
The neighboring town...

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.650
On my bike, we'll get there in no time!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.340
This way!

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.890
Fashion Market Shimomura

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.890
Thank you very much!

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:32.060
I'm so glad they still had it in medium here!

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:37.270
The other store didn't have this.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.690
<i>I have a feeling...</i>

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.110
<i>...that she might be able to become...</i>

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.410
<i>...a Shimomura Master!</i>

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.570
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:31.090
I'm hungry.

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:35.260
We don't have any more snacks left.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:36.390
Ah.

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.680
We have seaweed.

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:47.110
She must've been really hungry.
